      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2016 Asian Pacific Society of Respirology.",
        "AbstractText": "Vocal cord dysfunction induced by exercise in children with uncontrolled asthma was identified by laryngoscopy. The paradoxical adduction of the vocal cords was also indicated by the breathing-related changes of the forced oscillation respiratory resistance showing prominent increase during inspiration and a large positive difference between inspiration and expiration. The breathing-related changes of respiratory resistance offer thus a useful first-line technique to diagnose vocal cord dysfunction."
      },
